<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

		<!--
    LawsLaboratory.Core
    _____________________
	
    Defines the fundamental domain concepts and mathematical abstractions
    used by the simulation.

    Core is independent of the application orchestration and execution
    mechanisms. It describes WHAT the simulation operates on, rather than
    HOW the simulation is executed.

    Main responsibilities:
      - Formula:
          Represents expressions, their elements, variable references,
          and their compiled instruction representation.

      - Laws:
          Represents the semantic rules governing the evolution and
          initialization of the simulation state. A Law aggregates its
          initialization, variation, and transmission rules.

      - SpatialModel / Value:
          Defines the fundamental spatial and value representations
          manipulated by the simulation.

      - Mathematics:
          Provides reusable mathematical abstractions required by the
          domain, notably probability distributions, random generators,
          domains, and geometric constraints.

    Architectural principle:
      Core contains domain concepts and mathematical mechanisms but does
      not orchestrate simulation execution. Higher layers may depend on
      Core, while Core should remain unaware of application-level
      pipelines, gateways, controllers, transport, or serialization.

    Initialization rules may combine a value distribution with an optional
    spatial distribution and an optional spatial domain. The spatial
    distribution determines candidate positions, while the spatial domain
    constrains the positions where initialization is effective.

    Laws intentionally remain a domain-level abstraction. Execution layers
    consume the compiled representations exposed by Core rather than
    depending on the internal structure of individual rule types.
  -->



  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="LawsLaboratory.Tests" />
	</ItemGroup>
	
	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="LawsLaboratory.Application" />
	</ItemGroup>
	
	

</Project>
